{"ts": "2026-11-27T18:15:43.442824Z", "run_id": "r-20261127T1813Z-f113", "unit": "openspec:add-web-ref-carry", "seq": 9, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-009", "id": "Q-009", "status": "answered", "reason": "The hold rests only on a generated test that failed at base and head alike and is not in the repository, so it cannot discriminate. The repository's own e2e test for the criterion asserts every observable of the scenario, and I read the page, the marker and refState and confirmed they produce those observables (two pages at limit 100 with the cursor, markers only for superseded and waiting, the status Badge the only badge slot). Consistent with the accepted Q-005 verdict on the same criterion.", "called": true, "tasks": [], "target": "H-d011c1bb", "kind": "verdict", "batch": "Q-009+2", "batch_size": 2, "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 0.813858, "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "3b88f9a6cc1f33f4108bb05375d0f6dc1363f8c9bc4b7f05415ae1c042bef311", "checked": [{"ref": "e2e/test_m8_ref_carry_grants.py:189", "quote": "@pytest.mark.l4(\"C-4b83877f\")", "claim": "The repository holds a browser test tagged with the criterion."}, {"ref": "e2e/test_m8_ref_carry_grants.py:204", "quote": "expect(superseded).to_have_text(\"superseded\")", "claim": "The test asserts the superseded marker on the ledger.create_payment@1 row."}, {"ref": "e2e/test_m8_ref_carry_grants.py:206", "quote": "expect(marker(row(page, \"acme.lookup_vendor@1\"))).to_have_text(\"waiting for approval\")", "claim": "The test asserts the waiting marker on the drifted server's ref."}, {"ref": "e2e/test_m8_ref_carry_grants.py:217", "quote": "assert queries(servers) == [", "claim": "The test asserts two tool-servers hits with limit 100 and cursor s2."}, {"ref": "web/src/tools/GrantsPage.tsx:126", "quote": "loadAllToolServers(createApiClient(), controller.signal).then(", "claim": "The Grants page reads all tool-server pages beside its other reads."}, {"ref": "web/src/tools/GrantsPage.tsx:219", "quote": "<RefMarker state={refState(grant.tool, servers)} />", "claim": "The marker follows the status badge text inside the same span of each row."}, {"ref": "web/src/tools/RefMarker.tsx:13", "quote": "if (props.state === null || props.state === \"current\") return null;", "claim": "RefMarker renders only for superseded or waiting, so current and unlisted refs get no marker."}, {"ref": "web/src/tools/RefMarker.tsx:16", "quote": "data-slot=\"ref-marker\"", "claim": "The marker is its own slot, not a badge, so the status Badge stays the only badge."}, {"ref": "web/src/tools/ref-carry.ts:347", "quote": "if (server.state === \"approved\") return listed.ref === tool ? \"current\" : \"superseded\";", "claim": "refState gives current or superseded on an approved server and waiting or superseded on a drifted one."}, {"ref": "web/src/tools/ref-carry.ts:91", "quote": "const PAGE_LIMIT = 100;", "claim": "The all-pages reader asks for limit 100 and at most 100 pages."}, {"ref": "spec:specs/web-tools/spec.md#scenario-superseded-and-waiting-refs-are-marked-beside-the-one-badge", "quote": "the row of `ledger.create_payment@1` has one `[data-slot=\"badge\"]` (`data-tone` `success`) and one `[data-slot=\"ref-marker\"]` reading \"superseded\"", "claim": "The scenario's observables are the ones the repository test asserts."}]}
